# FTOL1 - arg-less calls of the x87 register helpers: `FUN_00ec62c0()` / `Stamp()` = _ftol2_sse (0x00ec62c0, operand
# in ST0, int64 result in edx:eax) and `helper_value()` = _CIsqrt (0x00ec6040, operand and result in ST0). The decomp
# reaches those bytes by declaring the function that leaves the float in ST0 as void (MSVC then neither pops nor
# stores it) and calling the helper without an operand. Each site below names that function from the x86 code and
# its definition, gives it its float result back, and passes the result to fnvnx_ftol2_sse / sqrt. fnvnx_ftol2_sse
# is the SSE2 path of the CRT's _ftol2_sse (libcmt ftol2.obj: `cvttsd2si eax` once __sse2_available is set, as on
# every SSE2 PC): truncation to int32, NaN and values outside int32 give 0x80000000; inline, a few instructions.
# Under MSVC (tests/s1b/msvc/s1b_check_fi.h) fnvnx_ftol2_sse(x) is the compiler's own float -> int conversion, i.e. a
# call of _ftol2_sse with x in ST0, so the MSVC check proves the operand. Method: docs/PATCHES.md.

